From: Shirogane Tsumugi <artoriapendragon123@gmail.com>
Subject: power: supply: generic-adc-battery: backport v6.4 DT rewrite

Backport of the v6.4 rewrite (compatible "adc-battery", io-channels
named "voltage"/"current"/"power"/"temperature", monitored-battery),
adapted to the 5.4 value-semantics power_supply_battery_info API,
plus local extensions the upstream driver does not have:

- CAPACITY computed from the monitored-battery OCV table via
  power_supply_batinfo_ocv2cap() (assumes 20C)
- optional charging-threshold-microvolt / charging-hysteresis-microvolt:
  report CHARGING when the sensed voltage exceeds the threshold
  (charger pulls the rail above any possible battery OCV), with
  hysteresis (default threshold/100) so the status does not flap
- PRESENT/TECHNOLOGY/VOLTAGE_{MIN,MAX}_DESIGN for interface parity
  with axp20x-battery on the epass_p family
- charging_capacity_reliable sysfs attribute (always 0): OCV-derived
  capacity pins near 100% while the charger lifts the sense rail.
  Fuel-gauge supplies don't have this file; userspace treats a
  missing file as "capacity stays valid while charging"
